{"name":"Colusa Wetlands","hex":"#7f725c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wetlands","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wetland (“An area or region that is characteristically saturated; a marsh”)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wetlands"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wetland","blocks":[{"text":"A wetland is a distinct semi-aquatic ecosystem whose groundcovers are flooded or saturated in water, either permanently, for years or decades, or only seasonally. Flooding results in oxygen-poor (anoxic) processes taking place, especially in the soils. Wetlands form a transitional zone between waterbodies and dry lands, and are different from other terrestrial or aquatic ecosystems due to their vegetation's roots having adapted to oxygen-poor waterlogged soils. They are considered among the most biologically diverse of all ecosystems, serving as habitats to a wide range of aquatic and semi-aquatic plants and animals, with often improved water quality due to plant removal of excess nutrients such as nitrates and phosphorus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/330px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wetland"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg/500px-Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg/1280px-Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org